<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Rolfe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1585">1585</a>–<a href="/years/1622">1622</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Rolfe was an English settler in the Colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> who introduced a sweeter strain of tobacco around 1612, giving the colony a profitable export crop. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pocahontas">Pocahontas</a>, daughter of the paramount chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wahunsenacah">Wahunsenacah</a>, in 1614 brought a period of peace between the English and the Powhatan. He died in Virginia in 1622.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-rolfe.jpg" alt="John Rolfe" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. W. Glass · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pocahontas_Rolfe_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the same years <b>John Rolfe</b>, who had begun growing a sweet tobacco from Caribbean seed, shipped his first crop to England in 1614, and the tobacco boom that followed drove the colonists’ hunger for land along the rivers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/powhatan-confederacy">Powhatan Confederacy · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>John Rolfe's</b> sweet tobacco, first grown around 1612, gave the colony an export crop, and in 1624 the Crown took direct control.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-virginia">Colony of Virginia</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Heacham, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in Varina Farms, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=52.91,0.49&amp;year=1609" aria-label="Heacham on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4561 341 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of John Rolfe"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5011 611h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5011 611h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=52.91,0.49&amp;year=1609">What was here in 1609? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
